<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Lawyers' claim protest paralyses Serbian courts.</title>
<headline>Lawyers' claim protest paralyses Serbian courts.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lawyers striking to demand cuts in their state taxes claimed on Wednesday to have paralysed Serbian courts.</p>
<p>They said provincial lawyers had joined the protest begun in Belgrade last Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have blocked the courts in almost all of Serbia,&quot; Radmilo Milunovic, president of the protest committee, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said meetings with government officials had failed to reach a solution.</p>
<p>Belgrade lawyers started a seven-day stoppage over what they said were &quot;exorbitant taxes which drove many of them to the edge of subsistence&quot;.</p>
<p>The government was ready to change some taxes, Milunovic said, but &quot;many issues still remained unresolved.</p>
<p>&quot;If our demands are not met, the Bar Association will decide on Friday to continue the protest,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
